{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life","id":30661,"title":"Bargaining for eternal life...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-15T18:00:28-08:00","id":30661,"title":"Bargaining for eternal life...","content":"Can a demon, through a pact, make somebody immortal?<br /> <br /> Can a demon make a person young again?<br /> <br /> Can a demon steal a body from one person via a pact which is given to another? IE, sorta an Immortals style body-switch situation?<br /> <br /> Could a demon make somebody a Thrall a vampire, if they ardently desired an embrace? What about other major templates?<br /> <br /> Could a demon cure derangement, or make them stop?... even for the geartouched? As an appendum to this question, can the demon 'heal' people by stealing bits of the things that afflict them as cover augmentations? IE; an alcoholic neighbor ; could an altruistic Demon bargain for his 'alcoholism' and use that as a cover trait for some future identity, effectively removing his flaws?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the questions, new to this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T18:16:03-08:00","id":30665,"title":"","content":"I'd allow for youth as a pact Asset, of severity depending on the difference between the current and desired age. It's not a Merit, but that's the general wheelhouse Assets work in. Immortality probably requires the mortal to remain dependent on the demon - repeated pacts for youth, or the Raise Dead exploit. Bargaining for youth is either going to be temporary (shades of Dorian Gray) or, if made permanent, leave the human in heavy hock to the demon; the demon is likely to ask for something precious in return, since they can get away with it.<br /> <br /> Soul pacts aren't temporary body-theft, they annihilate the subject and replace them with a corresponding Cover for the demon. So I definitely wouldn't allow somebody to bargain away somebody <i>else's</i> soul. If there were three signatories to a pact, though, I could see somebody willing to bargain their soul away in exchange for an Asset given to the third party.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: Or did you mean a demon signing a pact for somebody's soul, then trading the uncashed pact to another demon? That, it seems, is kosher \u2014 it's a common trade in temporal Agencies, according to my reading. I'm not certain, though.</i><br /> <br /> I don't understand your vampire question; do you mean &quot;thralls&quot; in the sense of Demon: the Fallen, or the ghouls of Requiem? Descent doesn't really have &quot;thralls&quot; in the Fallen sense; demons get specific things out of pacts and yield specific effects in return, rather than a general state of thralldom. Demons can pact with other supernatural beings, and can even accept their souls in a pact and thereby claim their lives (or unlives), but the result is a Cover identity with the semblance of the supernatural being <i>as a mortal human</i>. This does mean a demon can simulate the resurrection of a vampire by destroying the vampire and &quot;becoming&quot; the vampire as a living human.<br /> <br /> Salving, or at least treating, a persistent condition also seems to me like a reasonable Asset - again, remember that pacts have a duration, and the Asset will wear off when the duration is over, or if the pact document is physically destroyed.<br /> <br /> Demons take aspects of life that take forms relevant to fleshing out an identity. So in corner cases, I'd go with &quot;yes, but&quot; \u2014 for your alcoholism example, I'd allow it, but it would come with everything attached to that person's alcoholism. If they made friends at the bar, they're your friends now, not his anymore. If he drank to forget, all that grief washes back over him again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-15-2013, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:19:44-08:00","id":31377,"title":"","content":"Huh, if you have a spare cover on hand and a soul pact with someone else also ready to cash in, could you &quot;gift&quot; that cover to the person who's pact you're cashing in?<br /> <br /> So say you have a cover, let's call it a Cowboy. Then you make a pact with someone who becomes a senator. Now you want to cash in that pact, so you take the Senator identity. Would it be possible to, instead of annihilating the person, to give them the Cowboy identity?<br /> <br /> Maybe this mortal is just really good at turning around cruddy covers. They get essentially eternal life out of the deal (constantly becoming new people) and you get to invest in cruddy covers and flip them for your benefit! Seems like a win-win kind of... in a way.<br /> <br /> Also, I just like the idea of some teenager working at a fast food joint reminiscing about the time she was a KGB agent in the cold war.<br /> <br /> (I should know this stuff, but the pdf is, like, six hundred pages long... I'm almost a third of the way done!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","user":"Kunoichi","date":".  Added more. 12-16-2013, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:59:44-08:00","id":31409,"title":"","content":"By default, no; the creation of a new Cover through a soul pact requires total annihilation of the signatory in order to create the senator-shaped hole to step into. I suppose theoretically the process might be able to be run in reverse (plot hooks!), if a human being can even step into a Cover-shaped hole, but, y'know, that would involve annihilating yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T15:47:16-08:00","id":31953,"title":"","content":"(Careful with the following links, you'll easily <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TVTropesWillRuinYourLife\" target=\"_blank\">lose hours of your time</a>)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life#post30661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a demon, through a pact, make somebody immortal?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Immortality\" target=\"_blank\">Define 'Immortal'.</a> Making someone into a mannequin, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AndIMustScream\" target=\"_blank\">unable to move, age, or speak</a>, would be one way to make them immortal. Or they could be <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SoulJar\" target=\"_blank\">stuck in a jar</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ResurrectiveImmortality\" target=\"_blank\">vulnerable to injury</a> while <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ImmortalityHurts\" target=\"_blank\">able to feel every injury every time</a>, simply <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AgeWithoutYouth\" target=\"_blank\">unable to die from old age</a>, or (my personal favorite of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BeCarefulWhatYouWishFor\" target=\"_blank\">be careful what you wish for</a>) <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/LifeDrinker\" target=\"_blank\">coming at a grevious cost to one's morality and sanity</a>.<br /> <br /> However you work out how exactly to <s>screw them over</s> fulfill the contract, taking the conceptual fact of their aging could be a part of the pact, I don't see why not. Since a character's aging doesn't have much impact in the timescale games typically pay attention to, off the cuff I'd say it would be a +1 factor for characters not &quot;currently feeling their mortality&quot; (such as senior citizens), a +2 for those who are nearing the end of their life or otherwise feeling their impending death. Different factors since it has different importance, and therefore a different impact on their life.<br /> <br /> I would say, however, making someone an Immortal, as in the template, is beyond a Demon's Pacts. I don't know if it's been said explicitly anywhere, but it's been the rule-of-thumb that one Template cannot make or strip another Template of being that Template.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life#post30661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a demon make a person young again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. Hand-waving it in, I'd say it's a +1 factor per age category they are youthened by. Actually, I'd say the other way works too, a kid who wants to grow up faster could bargain to be more aged. (&quot;Age categories&quot; might be a hold-over from D&amp;D for me, I don't know if they've been addressed in WoD. Nevertheless, infant/child/teen/young adult/adult/venerable.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life#post30661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a demon steal a body from one person via a pact which is given to another? IE, sorta an Immortals style body-switch situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If Demon A buys the Soul Pact made by Demon B, Demon A would effectively be stealing the body of someone who's never met Demon A in any of their forms or covers. If this isn't an Immortals-style body-switch, well, I haven't read Immortals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, giving someone someone else's life by transferring a Soul Pact to THEM, is suddenly an interesting idea. Demon A holds the Soul Pact of Johnnie Rockstar, and Joe the Plumber wants to be a rockstar. Plothook!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life#post30661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a demon make somebody a Thrall a vampire, if they ardently desired an embrace? What about other major templates?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if they convince the vampire to Embrace them. But through a Pact go *poof* and the person is now one of the Kindred? Nope. Same for other Templates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life#post30661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a demon cure derangement, or make them stop?... even for the geartouched? As an appendum to this question, can the demon 'heal' people by stealing bits of the things that afflict them as cover augmentations? IE; an alcoholic neighbor ; could an altruistic Demon bargain for his 'alcoholism' and use that as a cover trait for some future identity, effectively removing his flaws?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Taking someone's bipolar disorder, paranoia, etc., should be on the table just like someone's wife, sister, or occupation. As for Factors, hmm. +1 for Minor Derangements, +2 for Major Derangements. Keep in mind that if you enact the Pact, and therefore actually take the derangement, now YOU have the derangement. Hmm. That makes me wonder about having someone you trade the &quot;undesirable&quot; cover aspects onto, essentially dumping them. So, you give all these derangements to some poor shmuck instead of enduring them yourself. If a player wanted to do that, I'd say them taking the undesirable aspects would be the same Factors in their favor as those aspects were in your favor when you took them. (So that +2 in your favor for taking Joe's schizophrenia is now a +2 in Tom's favor when you make Tom's Pact, assuming you're giving that schizophrenia to Tom.)<br /> <br /> Not sure what you mean by 'geartouched', but if you mean Stigmatics, then it's a Minor Template. It's fuzzy if I'd let a Demon take someone's being a Stigmatic, (since enacting a Pact with a Demon could very well be enough to make them a Stigmatic right then and there!), but Rule #2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/30661-bargaining-for-eternal-life#post30661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for all the questions, new to this game.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lt. Worf, &quot;Rightful Heir&quot;, ST:TNG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions are the beginning of wisdom, the mark of a true warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T20:00:47-08:00","id":32919,"title":"","content":"Demons can take Covers from other Supernatural beings via Soul Pacts, but it's generally unwise, since they don't get the supernatural powers that go along with being, say, a mage. They don't seem to have any ability to turn someone into a supernatural being.<br /> <br /> That said, iirc, they can give people pretty much any kind of Merit, so some of the general Psychic Power merits from the GMC might be on the table, depending on the ST. They can also turn someoneinto the head of their Cult via a pact, so they can create and gather their own minions this way.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's all be default. Demon has a number of points where it reminds you that it's a guide to telling stories, not a straitjacket and, if you don't like something or want to do something that's not supported, you should change it or do it. Thus, valid answers to your questions would also be &quot;Check with your ST.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}